{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ZYzBqEHvUmqjeK7oNWbP9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"The Linux Foundation — official candidate-facing T&C DOCS, 'Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions'\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: []\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-exam-format\", \"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# Multiple Choice Exams: FAQ — Linux Foundation T&C DOCS\n10\t\n11\t> THIS SNAPSHOT CHANGES A LOAD-BEARING CHAPTER 1 CLAIM. See the Ch 1 research\n12\t> manifest, \"Corrections required before drafting\", finding 1.\n13\t\n14\tOfficial Linux Foundation candidate handbook documentation, not a third-party\n15\tsite. Governs the LF's multiple-choice exams as a class. The KCNA exam page\n16\tcalls KCNA \"an online, proctored, multiple-choice exam\", placing it in this class.\n17\t\n18\t## Passing score — PUBLISHED\n19\t\n20\t\"A score of 75% or above must be earned to pass the Multiple Choice Exam.\"\n21\t\n22\t## Duration — PUBLISHED\n23\t\n24\t\"Candidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA. CNPA candidates are allowed 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n25\t\n26\t## Question count — NOT PUBLISHED\n27\t\n28\tConfirmed absent on targeted fetch 2026-08-23. No statement of how many\n29\tquestions an exam contains, and none that the number varies by exam.\n30\t\n31\t## Scoring methodology — NOT PUBLISHED\n32\t\n33\tNo mention of scaled scoring, cut scores, or psychometric standard setting.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope caveat\n36\t\n37\tThe FAQ is titled for multiple-choice exams generally and does not enumerate\n38\twhich exams it covers. CNPA is named as a timing exception; the renewal section\n39\treferences KCNA, KCSA, and CKA/CKAD/CKS re: the CARE program.\n40\t\n41\tSupported phrasings:\n42\t- CORRECT: \"The Linux Foundation publishes a 75% passing standard for its\n43\t  multiple-choice exams, of which the KCNA is one.\"\n44\t- FALSE, do not write: \"The Linux Foundation does not publish a passing score.\"\n45\t- FALSE, do not write: \"The KCNA exam page states the passing score is 75%.\"\n46\t  (It is in the candidate handbook, not on the exam page.)\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"69196c12-7fa0-4ab3-901d-cfec5a123f96","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:30:37.684Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\lf-mc-exam-faq-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"The Linux Foundation — official candidate-facing T&C DOCS, 'Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions'\"\nobjectives_covered: []\nconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-exam-format\", \"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n---\n\n# Multiple Choice Exams: FAQ — Linux Foundation T&C DOCS\n\n> THIS SNAPSHOT CHANGES A LOAD-BEARING CHAPTER 1 CLAIM. See the Ch 1 research\n> manifest, \"Corrections required before drafting\", finding 1.\n\nOfficial Linux Foundation candidate handbook documentation, not a third-party\nsite. Governs the LF's multiple-choice exams as a class. The KCNA exam page\ncalls KCNA \"an online, proctored, multiple-choice exam\", placing it in this class.\n\n## Passing score — PUBLISHED\n\n\"A score of 75% or above must be earned to pass the Multiple Choice Exam.\"\n\n## Duration — PUBLISHED\n\n\"Candidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA. CNPA candidates are allowed 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n## Question count — NOT PUBLISHED\n\nConfirmed absent on targeted fetch 2026-08-23. No statement of how many\nquestions an exam contains, and none that the number varies by exam.\n\n## Scoring methodology — NOT PUBLISHED\n\nNo mention of scaled scoring, cut scores, or psychometric standard setting.\n\n## Scope caveat\n\nThe FAQ is titled for multiple-choice exams generally and does not enumerate\nwhich exams it covers. CNPA is named as a timing exception; the renewal section\nreferences KCNA, KCSA, and CKA/CKAD/CKS re: the CARE program.\n\nSupported phrasings:\n- CORRECT: \"The Linux Foundation publishes a 75% passing standard for its\n  multiple-choice exams, of which the KCNA is one.\"\n- FALSE, do not write: \"The Linux Foundation does not publish a passing score.\"\n- FALSE, do not write: \"The KCNA exam page states the passing score is 75%.\"\n  (It is in the candidate handbook, not on the exam page.)\n","numLines":47,"startLine":1,"totalLines":47}}}
