{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ZJQ3zcVDvZpTX3WkqiDkp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/kcna-program-changes/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"The Linux Foundation (Training & Certification) — KCNA program changes notice\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: []\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"blueprint-change-2025-11-24\", \"domain-weights-44-28-16-12\"]\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# KCNA Program Changes — Linux Foundation\n10\t\n11\t> CORRECTION 2026-08-23: the previous capture of this page listed the retired\n12\t> five-domain weights (46/22/16/8/8) as if sourced here. Targeted re-fetch\n13\t> confirms THE PAGE DOES NOT DISPLAY THE PREVIOUS DOMAIN STRUCTURE OR WEIGHTS.\n14\t> Those figures have been removed from this snapshot. For the retired weights\n15\t> see cncf-curriculum-repo-kcna-versions-2026-08-23.md — currently an OPEN GAP.\n16\t\n17\t## Announcement\n18\t\n19\t\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam will be updated no earlier than November 24, 2025.\"\n20\t\n21\t## What changed\n22\t\n23\t\"The KCNA domains (i.e. Fundamentals, Container Orchestration etc.) will remain mostly unchanged except that observability will be rolled under Cloud Native Architecture.\"\n24\t\n25\t## Which blueprint a candidate is tested on\n26\t\n27\t\"Any KCNA exam taken after the updated release will test on the new set of Domains and Competencies.\"\n28\t\n29\t\"It does NOT matter if the exam reservation happens to be for a first attempt or a retake, nor does it matter on what date you completed the exam purchase. The only date that matters is the date you sit for the exam.\"\n30\t\n31\t## Rationale\n32\t\n33\t\"These updates are part of our ongoing efforts to ensure that a Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) has the most updated skills, knowledge, and competence needed in the industry.\"\n34\t\n35\t## Updated domains and competencies\n36\t\n37\t- \"Kubernetes Fundamentals – 44%\": Kubernetes Core Concepts; Administration; Scheduling; Containerization\n38\t- \"Container Orchestration – 28%\": Networking; Security; Troubleshooting; Storage\n39\t- \"Cloud Native Application Delivery – 16%\": Application Delivery; Debugging\n40\t- \"Cloud Native Architecture – 12%\": Observability; Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles; Cloud Native Community and Collaboration\n41\t\n42\t## Not stated on this page\n43\t\n44\tNo question count, no passing score, no duration, and no retired-blueprint weights.\n45\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"5fb8bce4-5ff5-41bb-886f-cbc361fd9f9a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:31:04.421Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\lf-kcna-program-changes-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/kcna-program-changes/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"The Linux Foundation (Training & Certification) — KCNA program changes notice\"\nobjectives_covered: []\nconcepts_covered: [\"blueprint-change-2025-11-24\", \"domain-weights-44-28-16-12\"]\n---\n\n# KCNA Program Changes — Linux Foundation\n\n> CORRECTION 2026-08-23: the previous capture of this page listed the retired\n> five-domain weights (46/22/16/8/8) as if sourced here. Targeted re-fetch\n> confirms THE PAGE DOES NOT DISPLAY THE PREVIOUS DOMAIN STRUCTURE OR WEIGHTS.\n> Those figures have been removed from this snapshot. For the retired weights\n> see cncf-curriculum-repo-kcna-versions-2026-08-23.md — currently an OPEN GAP.\n\n## Announcement\n\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam will be updated no earlier than November 24, 2025.\"\n\n## What changed\n\n\"The KCNA domains (i.e. Fundamentals, Container Orchestration etc.) will remain mostly unchanged except that observability will be rolled under Cloud Native Architecture.\"\n\n## Which blueprint a candidate is tested on\n\n\"Any KCNA exam taken after the updated release will test on the new set of Domains and Competencies.\"\n\n\"It does NOT matter if the exam reservation happens to be for a first attempt or a retake, nor does it matter on what date you completed the exam purchase. The only date that matters is the date you sit for the exam.\"\n\n## Rationale\n\n\"These updates are part of our ongoing efforts to ensure that a Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) has the most updated skills, knowledge, and competence needed in the industry.\"\n\n## Updated domains and competencies\n\n- \"Kubernetes Fundamentals – 44%\": Kubernetes Core Concepts; Administration; Scheduling; Containerization\n- \"Container Orchestration – 28%\": Networking; Security; Troubleshooting; Storage\n- \"Cloud Native Application Delivery – 16%\": Application Delivery; Debugging\n- \"Cloud Native Architecture – 12%\": Observability; Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles; Cloud Native Community and Collaboration\n\n## Not stated on this page\n\nNo question count, no passing score, no duration, and no retired-blueprint weights.\n","numLines":45,"startLine":1,"totalLines":45}}}
