{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y9t5yF5WRF4oqvXPEPfTy5","type":"tool_result","content":"# Exam Details - Verbatim Extracts\n\n## (1) Exam Duration and Question Count\n**Duration:** \"Candidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA. CNPA candidates are allowed 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n**Question Count:** NOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\n## (2) Passing Score\n\"A score of 75% or above must be earned to pass the Multiple Choice Exam.\"\n\n## (3) Skipping, Flagging, or Navigation\nNOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\n## (4) Reference Materials, Notes, or Documentation Permitted\nNOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\n## (5) Retakes\n\"Candidates have the option to retake and pass the exam to renew their certification.\"\n\nAdditional context: \"Certification Renewal must be completed prior to the certification expiration date.\"\n\n## (6) Exam Interface and Question Presentation\nNOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\n## (7) Certification Validity and Renewal\n**Validity:** \"Certifications are valid for 2 years.\"\n\n**Renewal:** \"Candidates have the option to retake and pass the exam to renew their certification.\" The renewed credential \"will remain current for a further 2 years effective from the date the exam is passed.\"\n\n**Alternative Renewal Path:** Under CARE program, \"passing a higher-level exam will automatically renew Associate-level certifications.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"305def94-64f9-4cbf-83e8-c2ff894b4f85","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:31:47.174Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":10418,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Exam Details - Verbatim Extracts\n\n## (1) Exam Duration and Question Count\n**Duration:** \"Candidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA. CNPA candidates are allowed 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n**Question Count:** NOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\n## (2) Passing Score\n\"A score of 75% or above must be earned to pass the Multiple Choice Exam.\"\n\n## (3) Skipping, Flagging, or Navigation\nNOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\n## (4) Reference Materials, Notes, or Documentation Permitted\nNOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\n## (5) Retakes\n\"Candidates have the option to retake and pass the exam to renew their certification.\"\n\nAdditional context: \"Certification Renewal must be completed prior to the certification expiration date.\"\n\n## (6) Exam Interface and Question Presentation\nNOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\n## (7) Certification Validity and Renewal\n**Validity:** \"Certifications are valid for 2 years.\"\n\n**Renewal:** \"Candidates have the option to retake and pass the exam to renew their certification.\" The renewed credential \"will remain current for a further 2 years effective from the date the exam is passed.\"\n\n**Alternative Renewal Path:** Under CARE program, \"passing a higher-level exam will automatically renew Associate-level certifications.\"","durationMs":4471,"url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X9qzJhtHE1Cz619n6LVuUc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Linux Foundation certification candidate handbook multiple choice exam rules permitted materials\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Exam Rules and Policies | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-rules-and-policies\"},{\"title\":\"Candidate Requirements | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements\"},{\"title\":\"Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook (using PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform) | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2\"},{\"title\":\"Resources Allowed: All LF Certification Programs | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/certification-resources-allowed\"},{\"title\":\"Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc\"},{\"title\":\"Linux Foundation Credential Exam: Candidate Handbook | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook1\"},{\"title\":\"Certification | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification\"},{\"title\":\"Taking the Exam | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook1/taking-the-exam\"},{\"title\":\"Linuxfoundation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-candidate-handbook*\"},{\"title\":\"Linux Foundation Certification FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/about/faqs/certification-faq/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results for Linux Foundation certification exams, here's information about multiple choice exam rules and permitted materials:\n\n## Multiple Choice Exam Rules\n\nCandidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA, which allows 120 minutes.\n\n## Permitted Materials\n\nFor Linux Foundation Multiple Choice exams specifically, candidates are NOT PERMITTED to access tools, resources or external sites when taking the Linux Foundation Multiple Choice OR SkillCred Exams.\n\n## General Exam Conduct Rules\n\nDuring the exam, the Linux Foundation has a zero tolerance rule regarding anyone who engages in exam misconduct. Exams are administered under strict supervision and monitored during the live exam, and the session recording is reviewed upon completion. Any suspicious activity will result in consequences including revoking a passing score and restricting an individual's ability to take an exam again.\n\nCandidates are not allowed to write or enter input on anything outside of the Exam console screen, and must refrain from inappropriate or questionable behavior, including failing to follow proctor requests, looking off the screen, and using forbidden resources.\n\nAdditionally, candidates cannot have objects such as paper, writing implements, or electronic devices on their desk or below their testing surface.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"1f6435b0-b2b6-4a7e-8249-11fdee9848e8","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:31:50.479Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Linux Foundation certification candidate handbook multiple choice exam rules permitted materials","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017jzwDg36BiyeMa5frP2gYw","content":[{"title":"Exam Rules and Policies | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-rules-and-policies"},{"title":"Candidate Requirements | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements"},{"title":"Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook (using PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform) | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2"},{"title":"Resources Allowed: All LF Certification Programs | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/certification-resources-allowed"},{"title":"Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc"},{"title":"Linux Foundation Credential Exam: Candidate Handbook | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook1"},{"title":"Certification | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification"},{"title":"Taking the Exam | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook1/taking-the-exam"},{"title":"Linuxfoundation","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-candidate-handbook*"},{"title":"Linux Foundation Certification FAQ","url":"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/about/faqs/certification-faq/"}]},"Based on the search results for Linux Foundation certification exams, here's information about multiple choice exam rules and permitted materials:\n\n## Multiple Choice Exam Rules\n\nCandidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA, which allows 120 minutes.\n\n## Permitted Materials\n\nFor Linux Foundation Multiple Choice exams specifically, candidates are NOT PERMITTED to access tools, resources or external sites when taking the Linux Foundation Multiple Choice OR SkillCred Exams.\n\n## General Exam Conduct Rules\n\nDuring the exam, the Linux Foundation has a zero tolerance rule regarding anyone who engages in exam misconduct. Exams are administered under strict supervision and monitored during the live exam, and the session recording is reviewed upon completion. Any suspicious activity will result in consequences including revoking a passing score and restricting an individual's ability to take an exam again.\n\nCandidates are not allowed to write or enter input on anything outside of the Exam console screen, and must refrain from inappropriate or questionable behavior, including failing to follow proctor requests, looking off the screen, and using forbidden resources.\n\nAdditionally, candidates cannot have objects such as paper, writing implements, or electronic devices on their desk or below their testing surface."],"durationSeconds":6.9252301,"searchCount":1}}
