{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AvcFuTsiHdFhd7qHVHnTyR","type":"tool_result","content":"# Linux Foundation Certification: Allowed Resources Summary\n\n## Multiple Choice & SkillCred Exams (All Programs)\n\n**Key Restriction:**\n\"Candidates are NOT PERMITTED to access tools, resources or external sites when taking the Linux Foundation Multiple Choice OR SkillCred Exams.\"\n\n---\n\n## Performance-Based Exams\n\n### LFCS (Linux Foundation Certified System Administrator)\n\nAllowed resources accessed from terminal only:\n- Man pages\n- \"Documents installed by the distribution (i.e. /usr/share and its subdirectories)\"\n- Distribution packages (may be installed if not available by default)\n\n### CKA & CKAD (Kubernetes Administrator/Application Developer)\n\nBrowser access permitted to:\n- \"Kubernetes Documentation https://kubernetes.io/docs/\"\n- \"Kubernetes Blog https://kubernetes.io/blog/\"\n- \"Helm Documentation https://helm.sh/docs/\"\n- Task-specific Quick Reference documentation\n- CKA only: Gateway API Documentation\n- \"Review Documents installed by the distribution\"\n- Distribution packages\n\n**Search Restriction:** \"using the search function on https://kubernetes.io/docs/ is allowed, but you must not open external search results.\"\n\n### CKS (Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist)\n\nBrowser access to Kubernetes documentation plus:\n- Falco, etcd, NGINX Ingress Controller, Cilium, and Istio documentation\n- Same terminal/distribution resources as other exams\n- Same external search restriction applies\n\n### ICA (Istio Certified Associate)\n\nBrowser access to:\n- \"Istio Documentation https://istio.io/docs/\"\n- Istio Blog and Kubernetes Documentation\n- Task-specific Quick Reference materials\n\n### CNPE (Certified Cloud Native Platform Engineer)\n\nBrowser access to:\n- Kubernetes Documentation and Blog\n- Task-specific Quick Reference documentation\n\n---\n\n## Universal Requirement (All Performance Exams)\n\nResources must be \"used by candidates to work independently on exam tasks (i.e. not used for 3rd party assistance or research).\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"824c28a4-2061-4384-8723-7d52f634c083","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:32:04.479Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":10461,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Linux Foundation Certification: Allowed Resources Summary\n\n## Multiple Choice & SkillCred Exams (All Programs)\n\n**Key Restriction:**\n\"Candidates are NOT PERMITTED to access tools, resources or external sites when taking the Linux Foundation Multiple Choice OR SkillCred Exams.\"\n\n---\n\n## Performance-Based Exams\n\n### LFCS (Linux Foundation Certified System Administrator)\n\nAllowed resources accessed from terminal only:\n- Man pages\n- \"Documents installed by the distribution (i.e. /usr/share and its subdirectories)\"\n- Distribution packages (may be installed if not available by default)\n\n### CKA & CKAD (Kubernetes Administrator/Application Developer)\n\nBrowser access permitted to:\n- \"Kubernetes Documentation https://kubernetes.io/docs/\"\n- \"Kubernetes Blog https://kubernetes.io/blog/\"\n- \"Helm Documentation https://helm.sh/docs/\"\n- Task-specific Quick Reference documentation\n- CKA only: Gateway API Documentation\n- \"Review Documents installed by the distribution\"\n- Distribution packages\n\n**Search Restriction:** \"using the search function on https://kubernetes.io/docs/ is allowed, but you must not open external search results.\"\n\n### CKS (Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist)\n\nBrowser access to Kubernetes documentation plus:\n- Falco, etcd, NGINX Ingress Controller, Cilium, and Istio documentation\n- Same terminal/distribution resources as other exams\n- Same external search restriction applies\n\n### ICA (Istio Certified Associate)\n\nBrowser access to:\n- \"Istio Documentation https://istio.io/docs/\"\n- Istio Blog and Kubernetes Documentation\n- Task-specific Quick Reference materials\n\n### CNPE (Certified Cloud Native Platform Engineer)\n\nBrowser access to:\n- Kubernetes Documentation and Blog\n- Task-specific Quick Reference documentation\n\n---\n\n## Universal Requirement (All Performance Exams)\n\nResources must be \"used by candidates to work independently on exam tasks (i.e. not used for 3rd party assistance or research).\"","durationMs":5999,"url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/certification-resources-allowed"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gop9QDuGNnqABn7CRHUYy4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Exam Rules and Policies - Key Extracts\n\n## Exam Conduct Rules\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to communicate with anyone other than the Proctor during the Exam\"\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to read the questions out loud, to themselves during the exam\"\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to leave their desk or step out of view of the webcam, unless they have been granted specific permission by the Proctor\"\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to eat, drink (except clear liquids as per rule below), or chew gum\"\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to wear any electronic device in their ears, on their face or on their body unless medically necessary\"\n- \"Candidate must refrain from making excessive and/or repetitive noise\"\n- \"Candidate must refrain from covering their mouth and/or face\"\n\n## Desk and Room Requirements\n- \"Desk must be clear of all notes and electronics\"\n- \"Room must be quiet, private, and well-lit\"\n- \"No one other than the Candidate can be present in the room\"\n\n## Notes/Scratch Paper Policy\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to write or enter input on anything (whether paper, electronic device, etc.) outside of the Exam console screen\"\n\n## Score Revocation and Exam Termination\n- \"Any suspicious activity will be addressed and will result in consequences including, but not limited to, revoking a passing score\"\n\n## Breaks During Exam\nNo statements about breaks are provided in the source material.\n\n## Navigating/Answering Questions\nNo specific statements appear in the provided content."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"76e8fe07-4fc0-4faa-bb04-ec7db572b0d4","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:32:05.787Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4756,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Exam Rules and Policies - Key Extracts\n\n## Exam Conduct Rules\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to communicate with anyone other than the Proctor during the Exam\"\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to read the questions out loud, to themselves during the exam\"\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to leave their desk or step out of view of the webcam, unless they have been granted specific permission by the Proctor\"\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to eat, drink (except clear liquids as per rule below), or chew gum\"\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to wear any electronic device in their ears, on their face or on their body unless medically necessary\"\n- \"Candidate must refrain from making excessive and/or repetitive noise\"\n- \"Candidate must refrain from covering their mouth and/or face\"\n\n## Desk and Room Requirements\n- \"Desk must be clear of all notes and electronics\"\n- \"Room must be quiet, private, and well-lit\"\n- \"No one other than the Candidate can be present in the room\"\n\n## Notes/Scratch Paper Policy\n- \"Candidate is not allowed to write or enter input on anything (whether paper, electronic device, etc.) outside of the Exam console screen\"\n\n## Score Revocation and Exam Termination\n- \"Any suspicious activity will be addressed and will result in consequences including, but not limited to, revoking a passing score\"\n\n## Breaks During Exam\nNo statements about breaks are provided in the source material.\n\n## Navigating/Answering Questions\nNo specific statements appear in the provided content.","durationMs":4484,"url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-rules-and-policies"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KGR8JWwrfoTBAgJ7Zpbgvi","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pre-Exam Requirements (Verbatim Extracts)\n\n## System/Hardware Requirements\n\n- \"Supported OS: Please review the System Requirements, published by PSI, in particular the supported Operating System Information.\"\n- \"One active monitor (either built in or external) (NOTE: Dual Monitors are NOT supported)\"\n- \"The Linux Foundation recommends a screen size of 15\" or higher to support the ExamUI.\"\n- \"The Linux Foundation recommends a screen resolution of 1080p.\"\n- \"Reliable internet access\"\n- \"Microphone\"\n- \"Webcam\"\n\n## Internet Requirements\n\n- \"Ensure others on the same internet connection are not performing activities that use excessive bandwidth\"\n- \"A wired connection is often more stable and robust than a wireless connection\"\n- \"Turn off bandwidth-intensive services (e.g. file sync, dropbox, BitTorrent)\"\n- \"HTTPS connectivity to AWS S3 endpoints like https://*.s3.amazonaws.com/* is required\"\n\n## Room/Workspace Requirements\n\n- \"Clutter-free work area\"\n- \"No objects such as paper, writing implements, electronic devices, or other objects on top of surface\"\n- \"Clear walls\" with \"No paper/print outs hanging on walls\"\n- \"Space must be well lit so that proctor is able to see candidate's face, hands, and surrounding work area\"\n- \"Space must be private where there is no excessive noise.\"\n- \"If the room in which the Candidate is taking a test has a door, it must be kept closed.\"\n\n## ID and Check-In Process\n\n*No statements about ID requirements, check-in timing, arrival windows, or check-in duration are included in this document.*"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"9d20d0b7-b2f1-41fc-bcdd-513b8743d377","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:32:08.043Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":7589,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Pre-Exam Requirements (Verbatim Extracts)\n\n## System/Hardware Requirements\n\n- \"Supported OS: Please review the System Requirements, published by PSI, in particular the supported Operating System Information.\"\n- \"One active monitor (either built in or external) (NOTE: Dual Monitors are NOT supported)\"\n- \"The Linux Foundation recommends a screen size of 15\" or higher to support the ExamUI.\"\n- \"The Linux Foundation recommends a screen resolution of 1080p.\"\n- \"Reliable internet access\"\n- \"Microphone\"\n- \"Webcam\"\n\n## Internet Requirements\n\n- \"Ensure others on the same internet connection are not performing activities that use excessive bandwidth\"\n- \"A wired connection is often more stable and robust than a wireless connection\"\n- \"Turn off bandwidth-intensive services (e.g. file sync, dropbox, BitTorrent)\"\n- \"HTTPS connectivity to AWS S3 endpoints like https://*.s3.amazonaws.com/* is required\"\n\n## Room/Workspace Requirements\n\n- \"Clutter-free work area\"\n- \"No objects such as paper, writing implements, electronic devices, or other objects on top of surface\"\n- \"Clear walls\" with \"No paper/print outs hanging on walls\"\n- \"Space must be well lit so that proctor is able to see candidate's face, hands, and surrounding work area\"\n- \"Space must be private where there is no excessive noise.\"\n- \"If the room in which the Candidate is taking a test has a door, it must be kept closed.\"\n\n## ID and Check-In Process\n\n*No statements about ID requirements, check-in timing, arrival windows, or check-in duration are included in this document.*","durationMs":5222,"url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements"}}
