{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011hwqYpCKtapVRRHHbQik2w","type":"tool_result","content":"# Extracted Information from Linux Foundation Certification Handbook\n\n## Exam-Taking Experience Details\n**NOT PRESENT ON PAGE** — The provided content does not describe the exam interface, question navigation features, timer display, check-in procedures, or ID requirements.\n\nSpecifically absent:\n- Exam console/interface details\n- Ability to skip questions\n- Option to flag/mark questions for review\n- Navigation between previous questions\n- Review screen or question navigator access\n- Answer modification capabilities\n- Timer display information\n- Check-in procedures\n- ID verification requirements\n\n## Linked Subpages/Sections\nThe page references two linked resources:\n1. **llms.txt** — Complete documentation index\n2. **lf-handbook2.md** — Markdown version of the current handbook page\n\n**Note:** The provided excerpt only includes introductory content about The Linux Foundation's mission and certification program. The specific exam procedures appear in sections not included in this excerpt."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"789ed8a8-3699-4557-9dd6-ef0919dfffb8","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:32:21.177Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":1328,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Extracted Information from Linux Foundation Certification Handbook\n\n## Exam-Taking Experience Details\n**NOT PRESENT ON PAGE** — The provided content does not describe the exam interface, question navigation features, timer display, check-in procedures, or ID requirements.\n\nSpecifically absent:\n- Exam console/interface details\n- Ability to skip questions\n- Option to flag/mark questions for review\n- Navigation between previous questions\n- Review screen or question navigator access\n- Answer modification capabilities\n- Timer display information\n- Check-in procedures\n- ID verification requirements\n\n## Linked Subpages/Sections\nThe page references two linked resources:\n1. **llms.txt** — Complete documentation index\n2. **lf-handbook2.md** — Markdown version of the current handbook page\n\n**Note:** The provided excerpt only includes introductory content about The Linux Foundation's mission and certification program. The specific exam procedures appear in sections not included in this excerpt.","durationMs":3621,"url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ArbpH5eJzmU6MrGwUkbEEX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Linux Foundation multiple choice exam KCNA flag question review skip return PSI Bridge exam interface\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc\"},{\"title\":\"Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook (using PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform) | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2\"},{\"title\":\"Candidate Requirements | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements\"},{\"title\":\"Frequently Asked Questions: CKA and CKAD & CKS | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-cka-ckad-cks\"},{\"title\":\"Important Instructions: CKA and CKAD | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/tips-cka-and-ckad\"},{\"title\":\"Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) Exam + Kubernetes and Cloud Native Security Associate (KCSA) Exam Bundle - Linux Foundation - Education\",\"url\":\"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/certification/kubernetes-and-cloud-native-associate-kcna-kubernetes-and-cloud-native-security-associate-kcsa-exam-bundle/\"},{\"title\":\"Taking the Exam | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/taking-the-exam\"},{\"title\":\"Multiple Choice Exams: Important Instructions | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/important-instructions-mc\"},{\"title\":\"Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) - Linux Foundation - Education\",\"url\":\"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/certification/kubernetes-cloud-native-associate/\"},{\"title\":\"Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) + Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) Exam Bundle - Linux Foundation - Education\",\"url\":\"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/training/kcna-cka-exam-bundle/\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search on Linux Foundation KCNA exam features and PSI Bridge proctoring platform. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**KCNA Exam Format:**\nKCNA is a multiple-choice exam that confirms conceptual knowledge of the cloud native ecosystem.\n\n**PSI Bridge Platform:**\nThe online proctored exam is taken on PSI's Proctoring Platform \"Bridge\", using the PSI Secure Browser.\n\n**Exam Interface Features:**\nThe search results include information about the PSI Secure Browser interface for taking exams. The \"+\" or \"-\" buttons (zoom in / zoom out) on the PSI Secure Browser Toolbar can be used to increase or decrease the font size presented in the Remote Desktop. The Firefox browser window can be maximized or minimized by double-clicking within the browser header.\n\nThe Content Panel (the panel on the left-hand side that displays the exam items) can be resized by dragging the border that separates the content panel from the remote desktop.\n\n**Disconnection Recovery:**\nIf the candidate is disconnected from the PSI Secure Browser during their scheduled exam time, they can re-launch their exam from the \"Access\" button in the PSI dashboard, or double-click on the \"PSI Secure Browser\" application. The candidate will have to perform the self check-in process again, to reconnect with a proctor and resume their exam session.\n\nHowever, the search results did not contain specific information about flagging questions, reviewing flagged questions, or skipping and returning to questions in the KCNA exam interface. For those specific features, you may want to consult the official Linux Foundation exam documentation or PSI Bridge FAQ directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"44e9cfa7-3162-4279-880c-aad5882fb1a7","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:32:25.854Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Linux Foundation multiple choice exam KCNA flag question review skip return PSI Bridge exam interface","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KHB7xbXFCGuKedDH6dtBZU","content":[{"title":"Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc"},{"title":"Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook (using PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform) | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2"},{"title":"Candidate Requirements | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements"},{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions: CKA and CKAD & CKS | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-cka-ckad-cks"},{"title":"Important Instructions: CKA and CKAD | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/tips-cka-and-ckad"},{"title":"Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) Exam + Kubernetes and Cloud Native Security Associate (KCSA) Exam Bundle - Linux Foundation - Education","url":"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/certification/kubernetes-and-cloud-native-associate-kcna-kubernetes-and-cloud-native-security-associate-kcsa-exam-bundle/"},{"title":"Taking the Exam | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/taking-the-exam"},{"title":"Multiple Choice Exams: Important Instructions | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/important-instructions-mc"},{"title":"Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) - Linux Foundation - Education","url":"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/certification/kubernetes-cloud-native-associate/"},{"title":"Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) + Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) Exam Bundle - Linux Foundation - Education","url":"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/training/kcna-cka-exam-bundle/"}]},"I've completed the web search on Linux Foundation KCNA exam features and PSI Bridge proctoring platform. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**KCNA Exam Format:**\nKCNA is a multiple-choice exam that confirms conceptual knowledge of the cloud native ecosystem.\n\n**PSI Bridge Platform:**\nThe online proctored exam is taken on PSI's Proctoring Platform \"Bridge\", using the PSI Secure Browser.\n\n**Exam Interface Features:**\nThe search results include information about the PSI Secure Browser interface for taking exams. The \"+\" or \"-\" buttons (zoom in / zoom out) on the PSI Secure Browser Toolbar can be used to increase or decrease the font size presented in the Remote Desktop. The Firefox browser window can be maximized or minimized by double-clicking within the browser header.\n\nThe Content Panel (the panel on the left-hand side that displays the exam items) can be resized by dragging the border that separates the content panel from the remote desktop.\n\n**Disconnection Recovery:**\nIf the candidate is disconnected from the PSI Secure Browser during their scheduled exam time, they can re-launch their exam from the \"Access\" button in the PSI dashboard, or double-click on the \"PSI Secure Browser\" application. The candidate will have to perform the self check-in process again, to reconnect with a proctor and resume their exam session.\n\nHowever, the search results did not contain specific information about flagging questions, reviewing flagged questions, or skipping and returning to questions in the KCNA exam interface. For those specific features, you may want to consult the official Linux Foundation exam documentation or PSI Bridge FAQ directly."],"durationSeconds":7.768827700000023,"searchCount":1}}
