{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N4shdXkQeVKdKYpKkesibZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Multiple Choice Exam Interface & Navigation Details\n\n**Exam Structure:**\n- \"The multiple-choice exam is delivered online and consists of 60* multiple-choice questions.\"\n- \"Candidates have 90* minutes to complete the multiple-choice exam.\"\n- Exception: \"CNPA exam consists of 85 multiple-choice questions\" with \"120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n**Question Navigation & Modification:**\n**NOT PRESENT ON PAGE** - The document does not mention whether candidates can skip questions, flag them for review, mark for review, return to previous questions, or change answers.\n\n**Timer:**\nThe page references a timer exists (90 or 120 minutes depending on exam type) but provides no details about timer display or behavior.\n\n**Exam Submission:**\n**NOT PRESENT ON PAGE** - No information provided about submission process.\n\n**Allowed Resources:**\n\"Candidates are not allowed to have other applications or browser windows running except the one on which the Exam is being shown.\"\n\nThe page emphasizes what is **not** allowed rather than what resources are permitted, focusing on environmental and technical restrictions rather than materials allowed during the exam itself."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"2a99ce61-d52b-4423-982f-3c5a25ea5c64","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:32:36.045Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":8972,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Multiple Choice Exam Interface & Navigation Details\n\n**Exam Structure:**\n- \"The multiple-choice exam is delivered online and consists of 60* multiple-choice questions.\"\n- \"Candidates have 90* minutes to complete the multiple-choice exam.\"\n- Exception: \"CNPA exam consists of 85 multiple-choice questions\" with \"120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n**Question Navigation & Modification:**\n**NOT PRESENT ON PAGE** - The document does not mention whether candidates can skip questions, flag them for review, mark for review, return to previous questions, or change answers.\n\n**Timer:**\nThe page references a timer exists (90 or 120 minutes depending on exam type) but provides no details about timer display or behavior.\n\n**Exam Submission:**\n**NOT PRESENT ON PAGE** - No information provided about submission process.\n\n**Allowed Resources:**\n\"Candidates are not allowed to have other applications or browser windows running except the one on which the Exam is being shown.\"\n\nThe page emphasizes what is **not** allowed rather than what resources are permitted, focusing on environmental and technical restrictions rather than materials allowed during the exam itself.","durationMs":4303,"url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/important-instructions-mc"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HpnKNJPzVyeQqhYhoK4TbR","type":"tool_result","content":"# Verbatim Statements from Linux Foundation Exam Documentation\n\n**Check-in Process & Timing:**\n- \"Candidates must start their exam no later than 30 minutes after the scheduled start time.\"\n- \"Candidates can click on the 'Take Exam' button, located in My Portal, up to 30 minutes before the scheduled exam time.\"\n- \"The wait time to get assigned to a Check-In Specialist should not exceed 15 minutes.\"\n\n**ID/Identification Requirements:**\n- \"First and Last Name listed on their Linux Foundation ID account exactly matches the First and Last name displayed on the government-issued photo ID.\"\n- \"If the name on the ID is written in another language (e.g. Chinese, Korean, Japanese, Arabic, etc.), the name used for the exam must also be spelled in that language.\"\n- \"You will be prompted to upload a picture of a valid government-issued ID, with a signature.\"\n- \"You will be prompted to take a 'selfie' which will be used to compare with the photo shown on your Government issued ID.\"\n\n**Exam Timer & Check-in Duration:**\n- \"The system does not offer a way to pause the exam timer or to add time back to the exam during connection loss events.\"\n- NOT PRESENT ON PAGE: Whether check-in time counts against the exam timer.\n\n**Exam Interface & Navigation:**\n- NOT PRESENT ON PAGE: Information about the exam interface, question navigation, flagging questions, or reviewing answers."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d388d963-c143-4111-9729-fe2603d659a3","uuid":"e3919f2b-a49a-4bda-b698-023b00e74253","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:32:38.900Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":7662,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Verbatim Statements from Linux Foundation Exam Documentation\n\n**Check-in Process & Timing:**\n- \"Candidates must start their exam no later than 30 minutes after the scheduled start time.\"\n- \"Candidates can click on the 'Take Exam' button, located in My Portal, up to 30 minutes before the scheduled exam time.\"\n- \"The wait time to get assigned to a Check-In Specialist should not exceed 15 minutes.\"\n\n**ID/Identification Requirements:**\n- \"First and Last Name listed on their Linux Foundation ID account exactly matches the First and Last name displayed on the government-issued photo ID.\"\n- \"If the name on the ID is written in another language (e.g. Chinese, Korean, Japanese, Arabic, etc.), the name used for the exam must also be spelled in that language.\"\n- \"You will be prompted to upload a picture of a valid government-issued ID, with a signature.\"\n- \"You will be prompted to take a 'selfie' which will be used to compare with the photo shown on your Government issued ID.\"\n\n**Exam Timer & Check-in Duration:**\n- \"The system does not offer a way to pause the exam timer or to add time back to the exam during connection loss events.\"\n- NOT PRESENT ON PAGE: Whether check-in time counts against the exam timer.\n\n**Exam Interface & Navigation:**\n- NOT PRESENT ON PAGE: Information about the exam interface, question navigation, flagging questions, or reviewing answers.","durationMs":5224,"url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/taking-the-exam"}}
